      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Ventricular assist devices are increasingly being used for mechanical support in patients with advanced heart failure. However, thromboembolism remains a leading cause of mortality in this population. We describe the successful treatment of native aortic valve thrombosis with bivalirudin in a patient with factor V Leiden mutation, who had undergone left ventricular assist device implantation, preventing the need for further surgical intervention."},
